\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.1}{\ignorespaces Compartment-specific inhibition of a single pyramidal cell. PV cells, shown as two separate types, inhibit the perisomatic output compartment, with basket cells acting at the soma and proximal dendrites and chandelier cells at the axon initial segment (AIS); there they control the gain and timing of spike output. SST Martinotti cells send an ascending axon into layer~1 and inhibit the apical tuft, the input compartment on which top-down feedback arrives. VIP cells inhibit SST cells and, more weakly, PV cells (dashed); when long-range or neuromodulatory input activates VIP cells, the tuft is released from SST inhibition (the VIP~$\rightarrow $~SST~$\rightarrow $~pyramidal disinhibitory motif). Neurogliaform cells in layer~1 add slow, diffuse inhibition of the tuft by volume transmission (dotted). Ascending feedforward excitation, arriving directly from the thalamus or relayed through layer~4, reaches the basal dendrites near the soma. Targeting follows \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\textcite {tremblay2016}.}}{7}{figure.1.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:interneurons}{{1.1}{7}{Compartment-specific inhibition of a single pyramidal cell. PV cells, shown as two separate types, inhibit the perisomatic output compartment, with basket cells acting at the soma and proximal dendrites and chandelier cells at the axon initial segment (AIS); there they control the gain and timing of spike output. SST Martinotti cells send an ascending axon into layer~1 and inhibit the apical tuft, the input compartment on which top-down feedback arrives. VIP cells inhibit SST cells and, more weakly, PV cells (dashed); when long-range or neuromodulatory input activates VIP cells, the tuft is released from SST inhibition (the VIP~$\rightarrow $~SST~$\rightarrow $~pyramidal disinhibitory motif). Neurogliaform cells in layer~1 add slow, diffuse inhibition of the tuft by volume transmission (dotted). Ascending feedforward excitation, arriving directly from the thalamus or relayed through layer~4, reaches the basal dendrites near the soma. Targeting follows \textcite {tremblay2016}}{figure.1.1}{}}
